# Pictures: kitty's graphics protocol, iTerm2's inline images. The runner's cell is 8 by 16 pixels,
# so 16 by 32 pixels (1,536 bytes of RGB: 512 groups of `AAAA`) are 2 columns by 2 rows. What is
# drawn is not on the screen text; these check where the cursor goes, what scrolls and what the
# terminal answers.

test a kitty image leaves the cursor right of its last row
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Display images on screen": the cursor moves to after the image (to its right, on the last row)
size 20 6
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=16,v=32,q=2;
repeat 512 AAAA
feed \e\\x
cursor 2,4
screen
||
|  x|
known-fail: alacritty – the graphics protocol is not read: the cursor stays

test a kitty image with C=1 leaves the cursor where it was
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Display images on screen": C=1 means do not move the cursor
size 20 6
feed ab\e_Ga=T,f=24,s=16,v=32,C=1,q=2;
repeat 512 AAAA
feed \e\\c
cursor 1,4
screen
|abc|

test transmitting a kitty image without displaying it moves nothing
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Transmitting images": a=t only stores the image
size 20 6
feed ab\e_Ga=t,f=24,s=16,v=32,i=9,q=2;
repeat 512 AAAA
feed \e\\c
cursor 1,4
screen
|abc|

test a kitty image at the bottom scrolls the screen to make room
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Display images on screen": the screen scrolls if the image does not fit
size 10 3
feed 1\r\n2\r\n3\e_Ga=T,f=24,s=16,v=32,q=2;
repeat 512 AAAA
feed \e\\
cursor 3,4
screen
|2|
|3|
||
scrollback
|1|
known-fail: alacritty – the graphics protocol is not read: nothing scrolls

test a kitty image wider than the rest of the line is cut and the cursor waits at the edge
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Display images on screen": the image is clipped at the screen's right edge
size 10 3
feed \e[1;9H\e_Ga=T,f=24,s=32,v=16,q=2;
repeat 512 AAAA
feed \e\\x
cursor 2,2
screen
||
|x|
known-fail: alacritty – the graphics protocol is not read: the cursor stays

test deleting kitty images moves nothing
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Deleting images": a=d only removes placements
size 20 6
feed ab\e_Ga=d\e\\c
cursor 1,4
screen
|abc|

test a kitty query is answered with the id
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Querying support": the terminal replies OK for an image it could show
size 20 6
feed \e_Ga=q,i=31,s=1,v=1,t=d,f=24;AAAA\e\\
reply \e_Gi=31;OK\e\\
known-fail: alacritty – the graphics protocol is not read: no reply

test a kitty query that is not quiet fails loudly and q=2 keeps the failure back
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Terminal Responses": q=2 suppresses error responses too
size 20 6
feed \e_Ga=q,i=1,s=1,v=1,f=24,q=2;AA\e\\
reply none

test an answer about an image keeps its place among the other replies
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Terminal Responses"; xterm ctlseqs DSR: replies come in the order the program asked
size 20 6
feed \e[5n\e_Ga=t,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=1;AAAA\e\\\e[5n
reply \e[0n\e_Gi=1;OK\e\\\e[0n
known-fail: alacritty – the graphics protocol is not read: the middle reply is missing

test an iTerm2 inline image leaves the cursor right of its last row
spec iTerm2 inline images protocol: OSC 1337 ; File = inline=1 : base64 ST shows the file where the cursor is
size 20 6
feed \e]1337;File=inline=1:iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABAAAAAgCAYAAAAAAAAA\a
feed x
cursor 2,4
screen
||
|  x|
known-fail: alacritty – OSC 1337 is not read: the cursor stays

test an iTerm2 file that is not inline is a download and shows nothing
spec iTerm2 inline images protocol: without inline=1 the file is saved, not shown
size 20 6
feed \e]1337;File=name=YQ==:iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABAAAAAgCAYAAAAAAAAA\ax
cursor 1,2
screen
|x|

# Animation and relative placements. The pixels are not on the screen text; these check what the
# terminal answers, and that the cursor stays where a relative placement is concerned.

test a kitty animation frame is answered like a picture
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Transferring animation frame data": a=f,i= sends a frame in the same way as the picture's data
size 20 6
feed \e_Ga=t,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=7,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=f,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=7;AAAA\e\\
reply \e_Gi=7;OK\e\\
known-fail: alacritty – animation is not read: no reply

test a kitty animation frame for a picture that is not there is ENOENT
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Composing animation frames": a missing image or frame is ENOENT; the codes are those of "Terminal Responses"
size 20 6
feed \e_Ga=f,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=7;AAAA\e\\
reply~ \e_Gi=7;ENOENT:*\e\\
known-fail: alacritty – animation is not read: no reply

test kitty animation control is not answered, and a missing picture is ENOENT
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Controlling animations": a=a with s, v, c, r and z; kitty answers it only when the picture is not there
size 20 6
feed \e_Ga=t,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=7,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=f,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=7,z=50,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=a,i=7,s=3,v=2,c=2,r=1,z=30\e\\
reply none
feed \e_Ga=a,i=7,c=3\e\\
reply none
feed \e_Ga=a,i=8,c=1\e\\
reply~ \e_Gi=8;ENOENT:*\e\\
known-fail: alacritty – animation is not read: no reply

test kitty frame composition checks its rectangles
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Composing animation frames": out of bounds is EINVAL; the same frame with overlapping rectangles is EINVAL
size 20 6
feed \e_Ga=t,f=24,s=2,v=1,i=7,q=2;AAAAAAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=f,f=24,s=2,v=1,i=7,q=2;AAAAAAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=c,i=7,r=1,c=2,w=1,h=1\e\\
reply \e_Gi=7;OK\e\\
feed \e_Ga=c,i=7,r=1,c=2,w=3\e\\
reply~ \e_Gi=7;EINVAL:*\e\\
feed \e_Ga=c,i=7,r=1,c=1,w=2,X=0,x=1\e\\
reply~ \e_Gi=7;EINVAL:*\e\\
known-fail: alacritty – animation is not read: no reply

test a relative kitty placement leaves the cursor where it was
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Relative placements": the cursor must not move after a relative placement
size 20 6
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=8,v=16,i=1,p=1,C=1,q=2;
repeat 128 AAAA
feed \e\\
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=8,v=16,i=2,p=1,P=1,Q=1,H=2,V=1,q=2;
repeat 128 AAAA
feed \e\\x
cursor 1,2
screen
|x|
known-fail: alacritty – the graphics protocol is not read: the cursor stays

test a relative kitty placement without its parent is ENOPARENT
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Relative placements": a reference to a placement that does not exist is ENOPARENT
size 20 6
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=2,p=1,P=9,Q=1;AAAA\e\\
reply~ \e_Gi=2,p=1;ENOPARENT:*\e\\
known-fail: alacritty – the graphics protocol is not read: no reply

test a relative kitty placement that would be its own ancestor is ECYCLE
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Relative placements": a placement that would create a cycle is refused with ECYCLE
size 20 6
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=1,p=1,C=1,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=2,p=1,P=1,Q=1,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=p,i=1,p=1,P=2,Q=1\e\\
reply~ \e_Gi=1,p=1;ECYCLE:*\e\\
known-fail: alacritty – the graphics protocol is not read: no reply

test a chain of more than eight relative placements is ETOODEEP
spec kitty graphics protocol, "Relative placements": an implementation must allow a chain of at least 8; past its limit ETOODEEP
size 20 6
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=1,p=1,C=1,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=2,p=1,P=1,Q=1,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=3,p=1,P=2,Q=1,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=4,p=1,P=3,Q=1,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=5,p=1,P=4,Q=1,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=6,p=1,P=5,Q=1,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=7,p=1,P=6,Q=1,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=8,p=1,P=7,Q=1,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=9,p=1,P=8,Q=1,q=2;AAAA\e\\
feed \e_Ga=T,f=24,s=1,v=1,i=10,p=1,P=9,Q=1;AAAA\e\\
reply~ \e_Gi=10,p=1;ETOODEEP:*\e\\
known-fail: alacritty – the graphics protocol is not read: no reply
